R1	`crc32` returns the CRC-32 of the message determined by the IEEE 802.3 generator polynomial 0x04C11DB7 — the same 32-bit answer that zlib, PNG and gzip produce for the same bytes.
R2	The nine ASCII bytes `123456789` must have the checksum 0xCBF43926.
R3	The checksum must be computed a byte at a time from a 256-entry lookup table, one lookup per message byte, and not one bit at a time.
R4	Messages of any length are accepted, from a handful of bytes to at least a few thousand, and every byte value from 0x00 to 0xFF may occur at any position in a message.
R5	The answer depends only on the bytes of the message: the same bytes give the same 32-bit answer every time, and no call leaves anything behind that changes what a later call returns.
